---
version: 2.0.2
title: enums: duplicate variants and enum superclasses
file: ./test/enum_semantics_test.gleam
test_name: enum_analysis_errors_snapshot_test
---
Source:
module main

enum Light {
  Red
  Green
  Red
}

class Loud is Light {}

---
error: duplicate enum variant
  ╭─ src/main.pooka:6:3
  │
4 │   Red
  │   ─┬─
  │    ╰─ first declared here
5 │   Green
6 │   Red
  │   ─┬─
  │    ╰─ `Red` is declared again here
  ╰─

Each variant may appear only once in an enum, so `Red` would name two values.

error: superclass is not a class
  ╭─ src/main.pooka:9:15
  │
3 │ enum Light {
  │      ──┬──
  │        ╰─ `Light` is an enum
  ·
9 │ class Loud is Light {}
  │               ──┬──
  │                 ╰─ only a local class can be inherited
  ╰─

Actors, enums, interfaces, external namespaces, primitive types, tuples, functions and generic variables cannot be superclasses.

Found 2 errors.

